      "text": "To find out how long it takes for the squirrel to travel 1 mile at a constant speed of 4 miles per hour, we can use the formula:\n\nTime = Distance / Speed\n\nIn this case, the distance is 1 mile and the speed is 4 miles per hour. Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\nTime = 1 mile / 4 miles per hour\n\nNow, we need to convert the speed from miles per hour to miles per minute. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, we can divide the speed by 60:\n\nTime = 1 mile / (4 miles per hour / 60 minutes per hour)\n\nSimplifying the equation, we get:\n\nTime = 1 mile / (4/60) miles per minute\n\nTime = 1 mile / (1/15) miles per minute\n\nNow, we can multiply both sides of the equation by 1/15 miles per minute to isolate the time:\n\nTime = (1 mile * 1/15 miles per minute) / (1/15 miles per minute)\n\nTime = 1/15 minutes\n\nTherefore, it takes the squirrel 1/15 minutes to travel 1 mile at a constant speed of 4 miles per hour.",
